{common:block}
    With the <b>&open;pad:content&close;</b> tag it is possible to define content for later use.
{/common:block}  

{pad:page 'content/1'/}

<hr><h4>Open or close tag</h4>

{common:block}
<p>If <b>&open;pad:content 'xxx'&close;</b> is used, then the content will not be processed before it is stored in the content store</p>
<p>If <b>&open;/pad:content 'xxx'&close;</b> is used, then the content will be processed before it is stored in the content store</p>
{/common:block}

